        <h1>How Shopify websites get benefit in ranking with page speed optimization.</h1>
        <p>
            Want to <a href="https://www.thinkwithgoogle.com/consumer-insights/consumer-trends/mobile-site-load-time-statistics/" rel="nofollow"> gain that 53 % traffic you are losing because of your slow-loading Shopify online store?</a> The good news is that you can really do something about it in a way more easier way than you may imagine! You can control the website traffic coming your way and can increase your Shopify store ranking with an exclusive <a href="https://www.pagespeedsolution.com/shopify-speed-optimization"> Shopify speed optimization service</a>. The following article will take you over some simple and easy strategies to implement to speed up your Shopify online store. We know this means a lot for your business because if your Shopify speed score rises, there is no one to stop you from having those big numbers and rapid sales. So let's just get started.</p>
        
        <h1>Best Tips To Boost Shopify Page Speed Performance</h1>
        <div>
            <li><b>Choose a Lightweight Shopify Theme</b></li>
            <p>Finding a faster theme to implement on your Shopify store works wonders. Faster themes have more concise codes, shorter load times, and minimalistic designs. They are usually clutter-free and simple. For example, Dawn is a free minimalist theme that always emphasizes speed and loads faster. Lightweight themes are built with clean and effective CSS, JavaScript, and HTML. You will get many such themes on the Shopify theme store. At the onset of your business, you can also consider choosing those themes that have already been tried and tested by your competitors or those having positive reviews. Also, you can install Shopify Theme Inspector, which is a profiling tool that helps you find JavaScript code lines that slow down your Shopify site.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <li><b>Disable Unused Apps and Plugins</b></li>

            <p>Another reason for a slow online store is keeping unwanted plugins and applications on the back end. The fewer the plugins, the better your site performance. Each plugin adds a data amount and code that needs processing when someone visits your store. A slow Shopify store needs an audit of plugins and its utheir in the store. You must know how many benefits all plugins and apps provide you with. Find out which plugin is slowing down your Shopify store. If you really need this, look for a faster alternative. Repeat the same process for applications.
            </p>
            <p>Plugins and applications are created in numerous ways. Some provide high-quality speed and good performance, and some might work in weird ways, eating up a large amount of code. 
            </p>

        </div>
        <div>
            <li><b>Use Lesser Shopify Applications</b></li>
            <p>Make sure you install only those Shopify applications that are really needed. Apps help add new features to your Shopify store; however, too many apps will affect its speed. Apps also help edit your Shopify store source code. On the other hand, they also consume resources for running. An excessive number of apps will hamper your Shopify store performance, and fewer apps will dramatically speed up online performance. </p>

        </div>
        <div>
            <li><b>Use Lazy Loading</b></li>
            <p>Just like image optimization, lazy loading helps slow down image loading time for large images. This is a very common technique applied by all website developers. Enabling lazy loading makes your website render only those images that your Shopify store visitor wants to look at currently. Any other images will remain under the fold and will not be loaded until visitors scroll down. </p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <li><b>Embed Product Videos</b></li>
            <p>Product pages must have both images and videos. Creating explainer videos can also impact your Shopify sales and increase conversion rates. Technically, uploading product videos can slow down your Shopify store. The best option is to embed these videos, as Shopify supports embedded videos hosted by a third-party platform like YouTube.
            </p>
            <p>In addition, embedded product videos always run faster than uploaded product videos. Hosting product videos on YouTube is a healthy sign of your brand credibility. With this Shopify store, resources don't get consumed. </p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <li><b>Avoid using Redirect Loops. </b></li>
            <p>Another tip is to avoid creating redirect loops on your Shopify store. This is also known as a redirect chain, which is a sequence of HTTP redirects. HTTP redirects redirect customers from one URL to another URL. A redirect chain has multiple HTTP redirects running in sequence. Since this is a technical aspect, you can seek site speed optimization service from a reputed page speed expert. 
            </p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <li><b>Get Benefit of Accelerated Mobile Pages</b></li>
            <p>Mobile accelerated pages are open frameworks designed to develop faster loading web pages on mobile devices. This feature helps boost the Shopify store collection page and other pages. It loads such pages in a fraction of a second. To use AMP, you get several Shopify apps with good ratings to help you. You can visit the Shopify store and find out options for the same and get them installed.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <li><b>Font Optimization</b></li>
            <p>We suggest you stick to a system font, as it also affects your store speed. If you use custom fonts that are not installed on the customer’s computer or mobile, then it may take time to download them. Sticking to a system font helps the rendering of your Shopify site, as the customer’s computer does not have to download additional fonts.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <li><b>Scripts optimization and website code</b></li>
            <p>Lastly, you can also speed up your store by optimizing code and scripts. Bloated or inefficient scripts will surely slow down your store's loading speed. As a beginner, you can remove unused JavaScript and CSS files. They add unwanted weight to the site. Another way is to minify your code by removing unnecessary things like spaces, line breaks, and comments from the code. It will eventually improve your loading speed. For that, you can use online tools like Minifier. If you need more experience with coding, we suggest you leave it in the hands of a trusted site speed optimization service. </p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <h1>Conclusion</h1>
            <p>At Page Speed Solutions, we have highly skilled and experienced page speed optimization experts to help you speed up your fantastic Shopify online store. As a team, we always prioritize speed and functionality at every project stage. We also monitor and optimize your site from time to time using our top-notch expertise. If you have slow page loading problems with your existing Shopify store or want to build a full-proof, speedy Shopify online store, then we have your back! We use the latest tools and techniques to deliver your site on time. Get in touch with us today!</p>
        </div>
